# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Run artifacts
# The dotted state spelling is named with its lock (Batch 89; closing sweep F38-2): the lock on the
# next line already says this spelling is machine state, and a state file git does not ignore is one
# a stray `git add -A` publishes.
.tech-radar-state
.tech-radar-state.lock
# Any lock, not only the two documented spellings: a lock names the state it guards, so it
# sits beside whatever the state file is called, and it records the machine's hostname.
*.lock
*.tmp
.plan.json
.pool.json
.items.json
.research.json

# Run state and the deliverables a run writes: state belongs to the machine, and a digest
# is an output. Keep a digest you want by naming it outside these patterns.
tech-radar-state.json
tech-radar-state.json.lock
tech-radar-*.md
tech-radar-*.html

# Publication rule: docs/ ships only its design. Everything else under docs/ is working
# material that belongs to the machine that built the skill, so a stray `git add -A`
# cannot publish it. Keep docs/design.md, which is the specification that ships.
docs/*
!docs/design.md
